{
  "_doc": [
    "E-A MUTATION-COVERAGE MANIFEST (A+ tranche 2, bar 1 CORRECTNESS).",
    "Every correctness-asserting invariant test file (enumeration rule:",
    "tests/lint/mutationCoverage.shared.mjs) must appear here with one of:",
    "  kind:'mutation'  — a planted regression in scripts/mutation-sweep.sh proves the",
    "                     invariant reds (label = the check_caught* label there);",
    "  kind:'rationale' — a documented reason mutation-testing is redundant or",
    "                     disproportionate (ref resolves in 'rationales' below);",
    "  kind:'uncovered' — a known gap, counted against uncoveredBaseline (shrink-only,",
    "                     exact-equality: drive toward 0 by upgrading entries).",
    "The 'meta' section carries non-test-file invariants (eslint config bans) the",
    "sweep proves directly. tests/lint/mutationCoverageManifest.test.js enforces:",
    "new invariant with no entry REDS; stale entry REDS; label claims match the",
    "sweep script bidirectionally; uncovered count matches the baseline exactly."
  ],
  "uncoveredBaseline": 199,
  "rationales": {
    "pglite-executed": "Executed-SQL boundary test: it loads the real migration SQL into pglite and asserts behavior by EXECUTION — the stronger form of proof this sweep approximates for source-scan invariants. Its mutation target is committed migration SQL; transiently mutating shared migration files risks discarding parallel-session work, and each pglite boot is heavy, so standing family-level mutation proof lives in the sweep areas security/runIf migration renumber, security/verify_jwt platform gate loosened, and security/public table without RLS. Per-suite mutation proofs were executed at build time (each suite’s Done-when in docs/A_PLUS_ROADMAP.md).",
    "golden-byte-pin": "Same-seed golden byte/structure pin over the full seeded pipeline. Its catching power is exercised operationally: legitimate behavior shifts redden the affected goldens and are recorded in the golden-shift ledgers (docs/GOLDEN_SHIFT_LEDGER*.md). A synthetic planted mutation would need a hand-crafted behavior-changing kernel edit per golden plus two full pipeline runs each in the sweep — redundant proof at disproportionate cost.",
    "self-proving-meta": "Guard-the-guard meta-test that injects its own broken fixtures (a fake failing tsc, a temp baseline) and asserts the enforcer reds — the mutation proof is embedded in the test body and executes on every suite run.",
    "walker-totality-executed": "Source-scan totality walker (E-D family) for the admin-actions two-key rule: its catching power is the exact-partition classification (every switch case in exactly one of PROTECTED / MODERATION / UNGATED) plus the client routing scan. BOTH mutation plants were executed at build time and proven red-then-green (drop a protected action from the manifest -> the unclassified-case assertion reds; route a protected action via a bare onClick runAction -> the client-scan reds). A standing sweep plant would duplicate that build-time proof at the cost of transiently mutating the shared edge-fn source each sweep.",
    "discourse-parity-variant": "Cross-surface lit-decade variant (tranche 3c) driving the discourse realizer over a real recorded DAG to prove its connected prose introduces zero unrecorded claims and zero contradictions vs the chronicle. The realizer's PRODUCT correctness is mutation-covered by tests/lint/discourseLexiconCoverage.test.js (the planted 'discourse/lexicon relation-type coverage gap' regression) plus the clause-provenance composition pin in tests/domain/discourseKernel.test.js; a second planted mutation here would duplicate that at the cost of a full sim drive per sweep. Its distinct value is the real-drive claims/direction/spell-break census, which a synthetic source mutation cannot target beyond the coverage the totality walker already proves."
  },
